\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
MUL _all_ UP _over_ SEQ 10
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are six Atoms.
 Our while loop starts at the right and whirls around.
 First,
 the integer 10 is encountered,
 and simply put on the stack.
 The SEQ command is then executed taking the 10 off the stack,
 and replacing it with ( 0 1 2 \SpecialChar ldots
 9 ).
 Now the adverb _over_ ‘knows’ to look for a command on its left—
here,
 UP—
which is applied to produced ( 1 2 3 \SpecialChar ldots
 10).
 Finally,
 _all_ similarly MULtiplies all of the values,
 pushing the result 3,628,800 to the stack.
 We’re done.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are two things we need to clarify.
 The first is what JEWEL[A[0]](A) does;
 the second is why we have the option to return(true).
 Let’s deal with that second wrinkle first;
 later we’ll devote an entire section to JEWEL.
