\begin_layout Section*
A single thread
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Modern JavaScript is effectively multi-threaded.
 You can deploy ‘web-workers’ to do things asynchronously in the background.
 When I started writing Zyzyxia two decades ago,
 things were more crude.
 If your code took too long,
 a confusing popup would invite you to kill everything forever.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So I built in the ability to fall back (return true),
 wait for stuff to happen,
 and then seamlessly resume.
 This has become a boon.
 It allows for great flexibility,
 quite apart from getting rid of those irritating warnings.
 Caution,
 there are rainbow details at this point I’m not going to dig into now.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Technically,
 asynchrony in JavaScript is plagued/haunted by the fact that async propagates upwards—
you can only await a result if your function is asynchronous.
 Bob Nystrom has an awesome rant about this if you want to plunge down multiple rabbit holes,
 asynchronously.
 If you refactor a function to make it asynchronous,
 this means you have to accommodate this in the entire tree that uses that function,
 everywhere.
 In JavaScript,
 Promises appear to help,
 but come with many liabilities,
 including the inability to cancel them.
 
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Section*
JEWEL?
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Let’s explore how we can possibly create an entire language with a single invocation.
 From above,
 you’ll recall this:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Quote

\family typewriter
JEWEL[ A[0] ](A)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Terse and almost sneaky,
 it says:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Look up a function that matches the type of the atom A,
 stored in A[0],
 and
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Apply this function to A.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
We can build our entire language with about twenty different types of Atom (Think of them as 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "codons"
target "https://drjo.substack.com/i/209344209/so-how-low-can-we-go"
literal "false"

\end_inset

